{{/*
  Telegram (parse_mode HTML) message for the War Room.

  Every alert line carries the labels that tell alerts apart (rule_group,
  pod, instance, ...), so a grouped "FIRING:2" no longer shows two identical
  lines; the first three carry runbook and dashboard links, and the first a
  graph link (the bounds below). The dashboard link opens on
  the incident: from an hour before it started to now, or to 15 minutes after
  it resolved. An alert without a dashboard_url (the charts' own rules) links
  to the Alerts board for the site that raised it, at Grafana's address next
  to Alertmanager's external URL.

  Flux events (flux-system/addons/alerts) carry their error text in the
  `message` annotation, so that is the last fallback for the alert line.

  The graph link is the whole expression of the rule, URL-encoded. Telegram
  answered ENTITIES_TOO_LONG (400) for each message of SecurityResultLate
  from 2026-11-15 23:11 UTC: two alerts, each with a graph link of about
  5100 characters, about 10500 characters of link text. Telegram does not
  state the limit (its error table says "too many styled message
  entities"). The bounds are chosen from two measured points, not from a
  documented limit:
  - refused: the message above, 10460 characters of link text;
  - delivered: the longest graph link of a rule that fired in the 30 days
    before with no Telegram failure is AgentPlatformCronJobFailed, 1444
    characters, 1643 characters of link text in a message of one alert.
    SecurityResultLate itself delivered only as one alert, before its
    expression grew: graph links of at most 1337 characters (2026-11-13
    and 11-14).
  The lengths are from observability/tests/test_telegram_message.py, upper
  estimates. So:
  - a graph link only on the first alert (the alerts of a group share their
    rule), up to 1500 characters in a message of one alert, and up to 1000
    in a message of more, where up to three alerts carry links;
  - the other links (runbook, dashboard or alerts board) on the first three
    alerts only, the ones that print in full;
  - the link text of a message at most 1700 characters, which the test
    checks for each alert of the repository in a group of eight.

  The first three alerts of a group print their text and links; the next
  five print their labels only. Eight texts of the longest rules (about 600
  characters each) would pass the 4096 characters that Telegram takes, and
  Alertmanager then sends a fixed line in place of the message.
  observability/tests/test_telegram_message.py renders each alert of the
  repository through this template and checks the limits of Telegram.

  Rendered with: amtool template render --template.glob=telegram.tmpl --template.type=html \
    --template.text='{{ template "telegram.message" . }}'
*/}}

{{ define "telegram.message" -}}
{{ if eq .Status "firing" }}🔥{{ else }}✅{{ end }} <b>{{ .Status | toUpper }}{{ if eq .Status "firing" }} ({{ .Alerts.Firing | len }}){{ end }}: {{ .CommonLabels.alertname }}</b>{{ with .CommonLabels.severity }} [{{ . }}]{{ end }}
{{- with .CommonAnnotations.summary }}
<i>{{ . }}</i>
{{- end }}
{{ range $i, $a := .Alerts }}{{ if lt $i 8 }}
• {{ if lt $i 3 }}{{ with $a.Annotations.description }}{{ . }}{{ else }}{{ with $a.Annotations.summary }}{{ . }}{{ else }}{{ with $a.Annotations.message }}{{ . }}{{ end }}{{ end }}{{ end }}
{{ end }}{{ template "telegram.labels" $a }}
{{- if lt $i 3 }}
{{- if $a.Annotations.runbook_url }} <a href="{{ $a.Annotations.runbook_url }}">runbook</a>{{ end }}
{{- if $a.Annotations.dashboard_url }} <a href="{{ $a.Annotations.dashboard_url }}{{ template "telegram.range" $a }}">dashboard</a>
{{- else if and $a.Labels.cluster (match "^https://alertmanager\\." $.ExternalURL) }} <a href="{{ reReplaceAll "^https://alertmanager\\." "https://grafana." $.ExternalURL }}/d/tnwks-alerts?var-cluster={{ $a.Labels.cluster }}{{ template "telegram.range" $a }}">alerts</a>{{ end }}{{ if and (eq $i 0) $a.GeneratorURL (or (and (eq (len $.Alerts) 1) (le (len $a.GeneratorURL) 1500)) (le (len $a.GeneratorURL) 1000)) }} <a href="{{ $a.GeneratorURL }}">graph</a>{{ end }}
{{- end }}
{{ end }}{{ end -}}
{{ if gt (len .Alerts) 8 }}
…and {{ len .Alerts | printf "%d" }} total, see Alertmanager.
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

{{/* The incident's time range: an hour before it started, to now or 15 minutes after it resolved. */}}
{{ define "telegram.range" -}}
&from={{ (.StartsAt.Add -3600000000000).UnixMilli }}&to={{ if eq .Status "resolved" }}{{ (.EndsAt.Add 900000000000).UnixMilli }}{{ else }}now{{ end }}
{{- end }}

{{/* Distinguishing labels only. rule_group paths are trimmed to the group name. */}}
{{ define "telegram.labels" -}}
<code>{{ range (.Labels.Remove (stringSlice "alertname" "severity" "prometheus" "container" "endpoint" "service" "job" "uid")).SortedPairs }}{{ .Name }}={{ reReplaceAll "^.*;" "" .Value }} {{ end }}</code>
{{- end }}
